{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And they shall go out, etc.</b> Around Jerusalem, for there is Gehenna there. All the sages learn from this verse that there will be a Day of Judgment in Jerusalem. Many say that ואשמם לא תכבה alludes to the soul upon separation from its body — if it was not worthy to ascend to the angels of HaShem, it remains by the sphere of fire. The ancients said that this is after the resurrection of the dead, and their proof is what Daniel said concerning the wicked after they awaken, that they shall be לדראון עולם. And all of them spoke truth:" "The word <b>לדראון</b> is like גדוף (reviling). Some say they are two words, and interpret ראון from the root of הוי מראה ונגאלה (Zephaniah 3:1). But לדראון עולם (Daniel 12:2) refutes them:" "Completed is the book of Isaiah the prophet. / Thanks beyond number to the Elohim of my father, / who taught me the book of his prophet and made my heart wise. / May He sustain my right hand to complete my writings. / In Iyyar of the year 4905 [1145 CE], in Loca, the city of my dwelling:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {2 "The acrostic of the four rhymed lines spells אברהם (Abraham), the author's name; rendered line by line without attempting to preserve the acrostic or rhyme. 'Loca' is the medieval name for Lucques/Lucca in Italy; confirmed by scholarly sources on Ibn Ezra's itinerary."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:23.044991043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}